# {{ project_name }} agent instructions

Write MMIX assembly in src/main.mms. Read tools/POLICY.md before editing.
Keep the project self-contained: only a C compiler, just, and Git are required
for validation. Never introduce downloads, external rule packs, language
runtimes, hosted scanners, containers, or checker suppressions.

Run `just ci` after changes. Treat assembler diagnostics as failures. Preserve
100% instruction coverage and update exact output and simulator state tests
when behavior changes. Put generated files only in build/ and never track them.

MMIXware is unmodified upstream generated C, pinned in vendor/mmixware.
Preserve its license and provenance. Do not modify the vendored source under
its original names. Local guardrail programs belong in tools/ and compile with
strict C99 warnings as errors. Compiler warnings from upstream K&R C are not
suppressed or presented as local guardrail failures.

The source model is a single executable, not a linker/module system. Do not
add an unvalidated second source tree. The host scripts use standard POSIX sh;
on Windows use Git for Windows with clang and just available in PATH.
